WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.919
You probably have gone to a pharmacy or doctor’s office

00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:06.680
and slipped your arm into a device like this.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.970
As the cuff squeezes and then gradually deflates,

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.600
it varies the external pressure on an artery in your arm.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.870
A sensor inside the cuff measures blood volume

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.230
in the artery and the machine uses this data

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.290
to calculate your blood pressure.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.560
Hypertension, or high blood pressure

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.820
is a major risk factor for heart disease

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.900
and strokes but it often goes unrecognized.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.950
In developed countries 45% of people with hypertension

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.460
aren’t aware of it.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.060
In developing countries it’s even higher--at 55%.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.740
That’s why many want to increase access

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.420
to blood pressure screening tools,

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.000
but the standard cuff method isn’t very portable--

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.180
not that many people own them in the first place.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:49.320
Now researchers have built a cuff-less device

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.460
to measure blood pressure that is convenient

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.020
and accessible.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.480
This new device uses the same principle as

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.499
the conventional arm cuff, but instead of a cuff varying

00:00:58.499 --> 00:01:01.539
the external pressure of the artery in your arm,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.140
the user varies the external pressure

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.960
by steadily pressing their finger

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.460
against a special case attached to a smartphone.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.590
The device is embedded with two sensors that measure

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:13.750
blood volume and applied pressure in the finger artery.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:17.229
The case transmits the data via bluetooth to an app

00:01:17.229 --> 00:01:19.740
on the smartphone, which computes the blood pressure

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.030
and provides a visual display to guide the user

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:23.560
and show results.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.340
90% of participants got the hang of using it

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.340
after one or two tries.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.170
the smartphone-based device was not quite as precise

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:35.119
as the arm cuff, but comparable to a finger cuff.

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.980
And it’s the first time this particular artery

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.440
in the fingertip has been shown to be an effective site

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.780
for blood pressure measurement.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.120
Because smartphones already have nearly

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.560
all the hardware needed for this method--

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.860
you could potentially ditch the case altogether

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.500
and just add a thin-film force sensor

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.500
atop the phone’s existing optical sensor.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.740
Another &nbsp;advantage of this system is that

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.820
many measurements can be made over time,

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.220
and then averaged to eliminate error from incorrect usage

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.720
or blood pressure variations due to stress,

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.980
physical activity, and other factors.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:08.960
Since it relies on the user

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:11.300
to actively press on the double sensor,

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.660
the device cannot be used

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.660
to measure blood pressure at night,

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.330
which is clinically important.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.800
The team still needs to test with a larger sample size

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.780
and they plan to add additional features

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.390
including an alert system

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:24.300
to warn users of high blood pressure

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.340
and securely transmit the results to caregivers.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.820
 

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.440
After more prototypes and tests, researchers hope that

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.890
soon you’ll only have to reach into your pocket

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.220
for an easy and accurate way

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.460
to measure blood pressure.

